{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.911aeea07e","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-171","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Priya Varga is a forest ecologist.</li><li>Varga wanted to find out whether fungi help trees share nutrients.</li><li>Varga added a traceable form of carbon to some trees and checked nearby trees for it.</li><li>Varga found that the carbon appeared in neighboring trees connected by fungal networks.</li><li>Varga concluded that fungal networks may move nutrients between trees.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Varga concluded that fungal networks may move nutrients between trees.","Varga found that the carbon appeared in neighboring trees connected by fungal networks.","To investigate the question, Varga added a traceable form of carbon to some trees and checked nearby trees for it.","Forest ecologist Priya Varga set out to learn whether fungi help trees share nutrients."],"answer":"D","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."}
